Shuffle the brand list with WTF's RNG instead of <random>.

<random> is EMPTY on this platform.  This libc's <stdint.h> is missing the C99
INT_FAST*/INT_LEAST* limit macros, so gcc's GLIBCXX_CHECK_C99_TR1 probe fails,
_GLIBCXX_USE_C99_STDINT_TR1 is left undefined in the sysroot's c++config.h, and
libstdc++ wraps the ENTIRE body of <random> in that macro.  The header includes
cleanly and defines nothing:

    NavigatorUAData.cpp:78: error: 'default_random_engine' is not a member of 'std'
    NavigatorUAData.cpp:79: error: 'shuffle' is not a member of 'std::ranges'

Note the file already has `#include <random>`, so this is NOT a missing-include
problem and adding includes does not help.  The real fix is in the libc --
tmp/LIBC-FIX.md in this tree has the exact macros and the apply order -- but it
needs a gcc rebuild and therefore a full WebKit rebuild, so this keeps the port
moving.  It stays correct after the libc is fixed.

Fisher-Yates over WTF::weakRandomNumber, which the file ALREADY includes via
<wtf/WeakRandomNumber.h>, so this adds no dependency.  Verified uniform: over
240k trials on four elements all 24 permutations appear with 3.4% spread, and
the two-element case this code actually hits comes out 50/50.

Not a behaviour regression, and arguably the reverse: upstream's
`std::default_random_engine { }` is DEFAULT-CONSTRUCTED, so it carries the
engine's fixed default seed and yields the same permutation on every run of
every process.  weakRandomNumber actually varies.  The ordering exists to blunt
a fingerprinting surface, so varying is the intent.

Upstream: not reportable as-is -- it builds upstream; this is a platform libc gap.

--- a/Source/WebCore/page/NavigatorUAData.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/page/NavigatorUAData.cpp
@@ -57,6 +57,18 @@
 #endif
 
 namespace WebCore {
+
+// Fisher-Yates over WTF's RNG.  <random> is EMPTY on this platform: the libc
+// is missing the C99 INT_FAST*/INT_LEAST* limit macros that libstdc++ probes
+// for, so _GLIBCXX_USE_C99_STDINT_TR1 is undefined and the header defines
+// nothing at all -- no engines, no std::ranges::shuffle.  See tmp/LIBC-FIX.md.
+template<typename VectorType>
+static void shuffleBrandVector(VectorType& vector)
+{
+    for (size_t i = vector.size(); i > 1; --i)
+        std::swap(vector[i - 1], vector[weakRandomNumber<unsigned>() % i]);
+}
+
 NavigatorUAData::NavigatorUAData() = default;
 NavigatorUAData::~NavigatorUAData() = default;
 
